From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 44/53] ASoC: codecs: add the Samsung COD3035X codec

The audio codec inside the S2MPU08 PMIC of Exynos 7885/7904 boards: its
digital block is SPEEDY device 3, its analog block device 7, both I2C
clients of the SPEEDY bus driver, so regmap-i2c works unchanged.

Ported from the downstream 4.4 driver of the SM-T510: registers, controls
(same names, so Android's mixer paths still apply), DAPM and the power
sequences of the microphones, the headphone and the earpiece. The mic
biases are DAPM supplies now (the downstream machine driver counted their
users itself). Jack, button and water detection (PMIC interrupt, GPADC)
are left out.

ABOX gives the codec its master clock and is never suspended, and the
codec's supplies are always on, so the codec stays powered: no runtime
PM, no register cache restore. The downstream write of 0x7D is dropped:
that register is not in its map, so it never reached the codec.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
